class: runtime
profiles: standard
summary: a Linux program linked with --link=libc, where compiler.c_runtime is true, looks root and group zero up by ID and by name through the C library and NSS rather than reading /etc/passwd and /etc/group itself, finds the process's own account by name when it has one, and refuses an ID and a name no database holds, a name holding a colon and a buffer too small with ERANGE, and a name longer than any system's LOGIN_NAME_MAX with no_account, as runtime/posix-accounts does on a static one; the C library is given the caller's whole buffer, so group zero is found in exactly the smallest buffer in which the C library finds it both there and past the group's joined copy, each measured at the address it is given, since glibc's need depends on the buffer's alignment and on whether nscd or its files answer
program: main.ldn
root: ../../../../..
link: libc
status: 42
constructs: 0940, 1030, 1660
targets: linux-x86-64, linux-arm64, linux-rv64
